      ],
      "source": "https://destinationpepin.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village name comes from Pierre and Jean Pepin, French explorers who traded in the area centuries ago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "King Louis XIII of France once granted a large area of the Upper Mississippi River Valley to two French brothers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepin%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Little House Wayside features a replica of the home where Laura Ingalls Wilder was born.",
